  "objective_check": {
    "algebra": "B_acc = M * (RECORD_B - s*PLANE_B*(1-overread)) / a",
    "d_prefetch": "Prefetch appears in B_acc ONLY through `overread` (pages it pulls that the skip verdict omits). dB_acc/d(overread) = +M*s*PLANE_B/a >= 0.",
    "conclusion": "Prefetch has NO byte-reducing term. It changes WHEN a page is read, never WHETHER. Hence gain(B) == 0 and gain(A+B) == gain(A) identically, so interaction = gain(A+B)-gain(A)-gain(B) == 0 for every operating point, and strictly < 0 with any over-read. This is a structural result, not a measurement: no trace, no tail size, and no cache capacity can make it positive on the bytes/accepted-token objective. Prefetch can only buy LATENCY hiding, which is a different objective and is already bandwidth-saturated per the 100% I/O-bound verifier finding."
